course: dictionary
lesson: 1432
title: Carousel: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. A carousel can be a fairground ride, a moving belt at an airport, or a set of pictures that turn one after another on a screen. Context tells you which one is meant.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Bags are tagged with barcodes and sent along kilometres of hidden belts to the right plane; nobody should ever climb on the baggage carousel.» Bags, belts and plane all point to a moving belt that carries luggage round at an airport.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. Could you say «nobody should ever climb on the fairground ride» here? It would not fit the bags and the plane, so the airport meaning is the right one.
fact: A carousel is a fairground ride with model horses or seats that go round and round to music, also called a merry-go-round.
fact: A carousel can also be a moving belt at an airport that brings passengers' luggage round.
fact: A carousel can be a set of pictures or items on a website or slide show that turn one after another.
fact: In «Bags are tagged with barcodes and sent along kilometres of hidden belts to the right plane; nobody should ever climb on the baggage carousel», the word baggage shows the airport meaning.
fact: A carousel turning round is an example of a circle: a full turn is 360°.
exercise: «Bags are tagged with barcodes and sent along kilometres of hidden belts to the right plane; nobody should ever climb on the baggage carousel.» What is the baggage carousel? | *A moving belt that carries bags round at an airport | A fairground ride with painted horses | A set of pictures that turn on a website | A kind of heavy suitcase
exercise: Mia says, «Let's ride the carousel!» at the fair. What does carousel mean here? | A small wooden box | A moving belt at the airport | A slide show on a screen | *A fairground ride with model horses that go round to music
exercise: Ben looks at a picture carousel on a website. What does this mean? | A round table for six people | A ride with painted horses | *A set of pictures that turn one after another | A belt at an airport
test: Which word in «Bags are tagged with barcodes and sent along kilometres of hidden belts to the right plane» tells you the carousel carries bags along? | plane | tagged | *belts | barcodes
test: A full turn of a carousel is how many degrees? | 45° | 90° | 180° | *360°
exam: In «nobody should ever climb on the baggage carousel», which meaning of carousel fits best? | A round wooden table | *A moving belt at an airport | A set of turning pictures | A fairground ride with music
